; (F4d) STOP (0F 9E; README "F4 (part D)"). Measured on the socket (validation/v35s/dma.py
; f4_stop, receipts f4-f4_stop-socket{,-2}.json): the CPU goes quiet (no bus cycle) until NMI;
; the first cycle after it comes 2^19 + 38 clocks after NMI's edge (the oscillator's settling
; count), into the NMI handler with IE 1 or 0; an unmasked INTP0 edge during STOP neither
; releases it nor is remembered (its IF stays 0). STOP does not set STBC's SBF (a store sets it).
; The routine is HALT's with the halt word marked STOP's by the counter field's last value
; (cnt=stop: no counter load): v35_top then releases the halted stall on its own count after
; NMI instead of the controller's wake, and holds the INTP samplers while stopped. The release
; pops the instruction after STOP, whose dispatch takes NMI. This file sorts last (after
; xfer_dma.uasm): no other routine's ROM address moves.
routine stop op=9E page=0f why="(F4d) STOP: HALT's stall released by NMI alone, 2^19 clocks after it (f4_stop); function only"
    halt cnt=stop                           ; halted (STOP's: v35_top's release, NMI and the settling count)
    e                                       ; E: the instruction after STOP (its dispatch takes NMI)
